protestors in Port Saeed determined to  continue what happened in cities  nationwide on Friday night the rare  showed dissent ended when riot police  moved in one officer in Cairo urging his  men not to open fire on demonstrators  demanding the resignation of President  Abdel Fattah el-sisi some arrests were  made including this man in Suez overall  analysts say Egyptian security forces  were uncharacteristically restrained  there was a full night of protests they  were across several big governor it's a  lot of people participated and the  people are just going to be emboldened  emboldened by the fact that they were  able to get away with it that they went  out into the streets they weren't  arrested on mass they weren't shot at so  there's I think there's a significant  chance that this could that this could  build up anger at cuts to food and  energy subsidies has turned to outrage  after corruption allegations a former  military contractor says president Sisi  and military leaders have wasted  millions of dollars of public money on  building palaces luxury villas and  hotels  Muhammad Ali posted videos on YouTube  and Facebook earlier this month calling  for protests against corruption when  most Egyptians live in poverty his  message is resonating with many people  the people are starving my life savings  have evaporated why why does Sisi starve  us while he lives in luxurious palaces  why is he trying to humiliate us he is  supposed to be a public servant working  for us  Sisi he was in New York for the United  Nations General Assembly denies  corruption allegations describing them  as allies Sisi banned all unauthorized  protests after he led the military coup  which deposed president Mohamed Morsi  six years ago tens of thousands of  Egyptians were arrested and jailed in  the government crackdown which followed  Human Rights Watch is calling on the  Egyptian government not to repeat pass  mistakes urging leaders to protect the  right to peaceful protest in upholding  Egypt's obligations under international  human rights law authorities should  immediately release all those arrested  for solely exercising their rights  analysts say it's too early to say  whether the Army's relatively hands-off  response suggests some commanders are  sympathetic to the protest movement  either way they say Sisi should be  worried Victoria Gaytan be al Jazeera
 

